[aspect-panel] target=Story US-5 (register-conditioned semantic recall: turns of <=12 words skip semantic recall, substantive turns keep it; env HU_SEMANTIC_RECALL_REGISTER_GATE off|shadow|live, default off) of sprint sprint-better-than-human-2026-09-05. Review: `git -C /Users/sethford/Projects/h-uman/.claude/worktrees/sbth-us5 diff sprint-better-than-human-2026-09-05..sbth-us5 -- src include tests scripts` (commits 23cb82c07 + 58efb051a). Files: src/memory/semantic_recall.c (hu_semantic_recall_register_admits, hu_semantic_recall_register_gate_mode), include/human/memory/semantic_recall.h (HU_SEMANTIC_RECALL_REGISTER_MAX_CASUAL_WORDS=12), src/memory/retrieval/hybrid.c (~L865 gate after the semantic search, LIVE frees semantic_result, SHADOW logs), tests/test_semantic_recall_register.c (15 tests, 4 fixture-backed integration tests with stub embedder), scripts/eval_semantic_live_gate.py (--register-gate, --dry-run, classify_register, per-register breakdown, AC-5.4 leak check), scripts/test_eval_semantic_live_gate.py. Contract: stories.md US-5 + designs/US-5.md in that worktree. Prior gates: verifier r2 PASS (14320/14320, ASan clean, 5 ratchets green), critic r2 MERGE. Rules for panelists: read-only; ABSOLUTE paths; export HU_SEMANTIC_EMBED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1 HU_IS_TEST=1 on EVERY binary or harness run; NEVER contact port 8741 or 8743; the built test binary is /Users/sethford/Projects/h-uman/.claude/worktrees/sbth-us5/build/human_tests (use --filter=register, do not rebuild); never open ~/.human/memory.db or ~/Library/Messages/chat.db; no message text/phones/contact names in output. Judge: correctness (gate placement relative to the byte budget and content filter; LIVE frees the semantic result without leaking or double-freeing; SHADOW output byte-identical to OFF); edge cases (NULL/empty/whitespace query, exactly 12 vs 13 words, multibyte whitespace, query_len shorter than strlen); security/privacy (log lines carry counts only; no text); regressions (default OFF path unchanged in hybrid.c; every other hybrid.c test still passes; harness default flags unchanged for existing callers in scripts/ and launchd job docs); maintainability (constant kept in sync between C and Python by a test). aspects=['correctness', 'edge-case', 'security', 'regression', 'style']
